  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274762/assets/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the minimum of the function is $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and it is reached at $x=-1.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the minimum point of the function are $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$",
